<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rogozen Treasure</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th–4th century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rogozen Treasure is a hoard of 165 Thracian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> vessels, many partly gilded, found in 1985–1986 near the village of Rogozen in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. Dating mainly from the 5th and 4th centuries BCE, it includes phialai, jugs and cups, several inscribed with the names of Odrysian kings such as Cotys I and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cersobleptes">Kersebleptes</a>. It is the largest Thracian treasure yet found.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rogozen-treasure.jpg" alt="Rogozen Treasure" width="320" height="330" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daznaempoveche · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rogozen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
